e","description","formalization_strategy","component","rationale","verification.assurance_level","verification.formalization_status"],"clause":{"candidate":{"description":"Users see the notifications that applications and web pages send. The shell shows each notification as a card with its title and its message, and it keeps a history of them. For a web notification from a page on a named host, the card shows the message of the page. It does not show the address of the page that the browser adds before the message."}},"component":"notifications","id":"STK-REQ-261004-6HJ2","title":"Users see the notifications that applications and web pages send. The shell shows each notification as a card with its title and its message, and it keeps a history of them. For a web notification from a page on a named host, the card shows the message of the page. It does not show the address of the page that the browser adds before the message."},{"changeStatus":"added","changedFields":["status","priority","category","req_type","fretish","description","formalization_strategy","parent","component","rationale","variables","traces.satisfies","verification.assurance_level","verification.formalization_status"],"clause":{"candidate":{"description":"For a notification from a Chromium-based browser, sanitizeBody removes the origin that the browser puts at the start of the body. The app name or the app icon must contain chrom, brave, vivaldi, microsoft-edge or opera; case does not matter. When the body starts with an origin link, sanitizeBody removes only that link and the white space around it. It keeps the rest of the body, which is the message. This holds also when the message starts with a web address or a dotted word, such as Node.js.\n\nA link is an origin link when its text is a host name with a dot. The host name has ASCII letters, digits and hyphens, and it can have a scheme, a port and a path.\n\nA body without an origin link loses a leading web address and the white space after it. That is the origin when the browser sends it as plain text. sanitizeBody removes image tags from every body first, and the card shows the result through styledBody.","fretish":"when chromium_sender & origin_link_at_start the notification_card shall immediately satisfy message_after_link_kept"}},"component":"notifications","id":"SW-REQ-261004-DHZ3","parent":"SYS-REQ-261004-74P8","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-261004-74P8"],"title":"For a notification from a Chromium-based browser, sanitizeBody removes the origin that the browser puts at the start of the body. The app name or the app icon must contain chrom, brave, vivaldi, microsoft-edge or opera; case does not matter. When the body starts with an origin link, sanitizeBody removes only that link and the white space around it. It keeps the rest of the body, which is the message. This holds also when the message starts with a web address or a dotted word, such as Node.js. A link is an origin link when its text is a host name with a dot. The host name has ASCII letters, digits and hyphens, and it can have a scheme, a port and a path. A body without an origin link loses a leading web address and the white space after it. That is the origin when the browser sends it as plain text. sanitizeBody removes image tags from every body first, and the card shows the result through styledBody."},{"changeStatus":"added","changedFields":["status","priority","category","req_type","fretish","description","formalization_strategy","parent","component","rationale","variables","traces.satisfies","verification.assurance_level","verification.formalization_status"],"clause":{"candidate":{"description":"When a Chromium-based browser sends a web notification with the origin link before the message, the card shows the whole message, from its first word. The card knows the browser by the app name or the app icon. When the origin is a host name with a dot, such as web.whatsapp.com, the card removes the origin link. Any other origin stays before the message, such as localhost, an IP address or a host name with non-ASCII letters.","fretish":"when web_notification_received the notification_card shall immediately satisfy page_message_shown"}},"component":"notifications","id":"SYS-REQ-261004-74P8","parent":"STK-REQ-261004-6HJ2","satisfies":["STK-REQ-261004-6HJ2"],"title":"When a Chromium-based browser sends a web notification with the origin link before the message, the card shows the whole message, from its first word. The card knows the browser by the app name or the app icon. When the origin is a host name with a dot, such as web.whatsapp.com, the card removes the origin link. Any other origin stays before the message, such as localhost, an IP address or a host name with non-ASCII letters."}],"intentEdits":3,"sources":["changeRequest.body","changeRequest.title","requirement:STK-REQ-261004-6HJ2","requirement:SW-REQ-261004-DHZ3","requirement:SYS-REQ-261004-74P8"],"status":"declared","title":"Keep the first word of a web notification's message"},"nextDecision":{"disclosureIds":["compat_change_unapproved:cf-2951ee28176c56d8","compat_change_unapproved:cf-ec0371b290a31db8","compat_change_unapproved:cf-ffe36b1d96ed7dba"],"kind":"human_judgement","question":"Approve each of the 3 backward-compatibility changes: a reviewer or above approves it, or the author fixes it.","reason":"compat_changes_unapproved"},"preservedBehaviour":{"requirements":[],"total":0},"readiness":"not_assessed","requiredAuthority":{"acceptedIdentitySources":["github_login","portal_user"],"basis":"approved_policy","enforcement":"portal_or_forge","policyDigest":"sha256:bc649c7377f819faae0f5f9526d0e5c06880645d5c0fab402effd0ac611da76e","policyRevision":"58cd8018b7ae7d6f96900e95c98b7d2fae3aacd0","role":"reviewer"},"routineEvidence":{"claimsObservedPass":0,"gatesAdvisory":27,"gatesNotApplicable":1,"gatesPassed":178,"testsPassed":10},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.decision-summary.v1","scope":{"approximations":["Function-level mapping comes from trace targets `path:symbo